ethan: quick report — intermittent "Unexpected end of JSON input" in node sdk when streaming large responses. Looks correlated with either client disconnects (user closes tab) or an auth token refresh that replaces the socket mid-stream. reproed in sample-app with node 18 + @redwood/sdk-js v0.6.3. anyone else?

maya: we saw something similar from the python side but it rarely surfaced because the python stream code concatenates more aggressively. node code currently assumes events arrive whole per data event which is false.

vikas: can you paste a minimal repro snippet + exact error trace? /cc @tori for runtime behavior during auth refresh.

ethan: minimal fetch-based repro:
```js
const res = await fetch(url, { headers: { Authorization: `Bearer ${TOKEN}` } });
const reader = res.body.getReader();
let buffer = '';
while (true) {
  const { value, done } = await reader.read();
  if (done) break;
  buffer += new TextDecoder().decode(value);
  // naive: split on double newline
  const parts = buffer.split('\n\n');
  buffer = parts.pop(); // keep trailing partial
  for (const p of parts) {
    if (p.startsWith('data: ')) {
      const obj = JSON.parse(p.slice(6)); // throws if boundary logic wrong
      handle(obj);
    }
  }
}
```
logs: `SyntaxError: Unexpected end of JSON input` with stack inside sdk event handler. I can reproduce by closing the tab mid-stream and by forcing token rotate on server.

tori: runtime note: when we rotate auth (refresh token), we currently tear down the TCP/TLS connection and open a fresh SSE connection without emitting any resume metadata. That means any partial event in-flight is lost unless client preserves trailing bytes across reconnect.

maya: another nuance: chunk ordering can change when proxies re-chunk; a single logical 'data:' event may arrive split across several TCP segments and even reordered in pathological cases during reconnects. We should treat SSE as a byte-stream and implement reassembly at SDK layer.

vikas: SDK parity follow-up: node sdk lacks a robust trailing buffer and tests for connection abort mid-event. I'll add an internal helper that maintains a persistent tail buffer across reconnect attempts and only JSON.parse once we detect the '\\n\\n' delimiter. Also add a boolean opt-in to enable strict sequence checks if server provides seq numbers.

ethan: runtime option would be great too: emit a small control event before closing due to auth rotate so clients can detect and resume. e.g. event: control
data: {"type":"pre-rotate","last_seq": 452}

 tori: yes we can emit a pre-rotate control event when we have a chance. If rotate is forced (e.g., 401 mid-request) we can emit a resume token on the new stream with last_seq echoed and let clients patch missing pieces.

alex: small workaround for sample apps and onboarding doc: increase token TTL for long streams or proactively refresh before starting a long-running stream. Also include a snippet showing persistent buffer across reconnects and jittered reconnect backoff to avoid thundering herd.

vikas: plan: 1) patch node sdk to keep trailing buffer across reconnects and only parse on '\\n\\n' boundary, 2) add unit/integration tests that simulate aborted sockets, delayed chunks, and auth rotate, 3) add telemetry counter `sse_parse_error` and `sse_resume_gap` so we can alert, 4) document workaround in sample-app and quickstart.

ci-bot: Created issue #4392: "sdk-js(node): SSE parsing fails on partial-chunk + auth rotate - add resume buffer & tests" assignee: vikas.

maya: for python parity please ensure both SDKs expose consistent event envelope when seqs are present: {"seq":#, "type":"delta","payload":...}. Clients should treat seq as authoritative for reassembly and dedupe.

vikas: agreed. I'll land the buffer patch first and then add optional seq-checking that errors if gaps are detected. Add a test matrix covering: proxy chunking, client disconnect, forced auth rotate, and slow clients hitting backpressure.

tori: runtime action item for us: minimize mid-stream forced 401s. If unavoidable, emit `event: control` with resume markers. I'll open runtime PR and coordinate on the exact JSON shape.

ethan: I will update onboarding guide + sample-app README to show robust streaming pattern (persistent buffer, retry/backoff, optional seq validation). Will also add a small troubleshooting blurb for parse errors and link to issue #4392.

vikas: ETA: patch + tests by EOD tomorrow; will also add telemetry flag so SRE can watch for regressions.

ci-bot: Issue #4392 updated: labels ["devex","sdk-node","sse","priority-high"], linked runtime issue #4393.

eathan: thanks all. follow-ups: vikas (sdk patch + tests + telem), tori (runtime pre-rotate control event PR), me (sample-app + docs), maya (python parity review). ping here when PRs are up and i'll smoke test with sample-app. :thumbsup:
